Hi Kim,

variogram.fit() is deprecated in favor of ctmm.guess(), but it likely won't make any difference here.
You generally don't have to fiddle with the parameters guesses. It only needs to be in the ballpark.
You should ultimately be using the fitted parameters. If they don't reflect the empirical variogram (within uncertainty), then there could be different causes for that. Feel free to post the output plots here. A big culprit is often non-stationarity and, in particular, dispersal behavior.
Best,
Chris

